WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.759
So we knew when we looked at the proposal
for Donald Trump's Republican tax cut last

00:00:04.759 --> 00:00:05.800
year, we knew from him

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.130
reading it that it would increase the budget
deficit.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.990
There are good and bad reasons to deficit
spend.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:13.400
We've debated some of those reasons before.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.250
What we have a almost unanimous consent on
is that deficit spending to give tax cuts

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:24.630
to the registered Americans is not an economic,
economically stimulative reason to go into

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:25.630
debt.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.610
So we knew it would happen and it has.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:28.960
The deficit has exploded.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.390
The numbers show it.

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:31.990
We've covered it before.

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:37.770
And so Donald Trump is now faced with exploding
budget deficits added to his China tariffs,

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:42.879
which have so deeply hurt farmers that the
federal government is now paying to bail them

00:00:42.879 --> 00:00:44.339
out as well.

00:00:44.339 --> 00:00:49.521
Just racking up even more deficits again,
as a result of the policies that Donald Trump

00:00:49.521 --> 00:00:52.269
has chosen, chosen to enact.

00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:55.639
So what is it that Republican Ted Cruz is
doing?

00:00:55.639 --> 00:01:02.379
He's demanding a tax cut for the rich expedited
without even getting congressional approval.

00:01:02.379 --> 00:01:10.189
Cruz sent a letter to Treasury Secretary Steven
[inaudible] asking that capital gains be indexed

00:01:10.189 --> 00:01:11.240
to inflation.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.329
Now this requires some explanation and I hope
that I'm going to do a good job of this because

00:01:15.329 --> 00:01:20.990
these things are not always the easiest to
explain, to understand how this is a tax cut

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:22.109
for the rich.

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:26.390
You have to understand how capital gains normally
work normally.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:32.570
Imagine that you buy $1,000 worth of shares
of stock and those shares of stock go up in

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.909
value to $5,000 the numbers are really clear.

00:01:35.909 --> 00:01:42.560
You paid a thousand it's worth worth 5,000
when you sell those shares, you have 4,000

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:48.079
in gains and you pay capital gains tax on
the $40,000 that's easy.

00:01:48.079 --> 00:01:54.450
Now to index capital gains to inflation means
that you add inflation to the purchase price

00:01:54.450 --> 00:02:00.130
of $1,000 so in our example, imagine that
you paid the thousand dollars for those shares

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:06.350
five years ago, and in those five years there's
been enough inflation that $1,000 then is

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.190
like $1,081 today.

00:02:09.190 --> 00:02:12.050
That's what I got when I used an inflation
calculator.

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:19.310
When you index capital gains to inflation,
you allow the cost basis of those shares to

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:26.230
be $1,081 instead of a thousand so what that
means is instead of paying capital gains taxes

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:33.761
on that full $4,000 you're only paying capital
gains on a little bit over $3,900 now, it

00:02:33.761 --> 00:02:38.500
doesn't sound like much with those numbers,
but that's what's important about this.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:41.360
This is a ton of money for the very rich.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.120
The reason that it is effectively a tax cut
for the rich is that for most people, indexing

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:54.150
capital gains to inflation is a difference
of just a few dollars here or there.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:59.560
86% of this action would go to the top 1%
okay?

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.200
Understand the scope of those numbers.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:09.140
86% of the benefit of making a capital gains
index to inflation would go to the top 1%

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:16.180
at a cost of more than $100 billion over a
decade, meaning even more debt, which Donald

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.430
Trump told us he was going to eliminate.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:24.450
The mere suggestion that this is an emergency
requiring executive action is laughable.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:28.840
Now, this is one of those cases, let me be
clear, I would love this.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:34.220
Over time more and more of my income has come
from capital gains of different kinds.

00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:38.990
This is a change that would be great for me,
but it's an immoral change.

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:43.910
There is no economically defensible rationale
for doing this at all.

00:03:43.910 --> 00:03:50.210
Nevermind the completely comical, farcical
assertion that this is such an emergency that

00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:54.930
it should be done by executive order rather
than by actually getting a bill through Congress

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:58.920
and signed into law in order to do this, which
they probably wouldn't be able to do because

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.940
it is such a capitalist's handout.

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:05.840
The funniest, or maybe the saddest part about
this is that Ted Cruz is actually touting

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:09.860
it as a way to quote help everyday Americans.

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:18.670
86% of the benefit from this would go to the
top 1% the bottom 99% would then split 14%

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:23.640
of the benefit, and by the way, I think if
you looked at like the bottom 90% they would

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:29.250
get a small portion of that 14% I assumed
the lion's share of that 14% would go for

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:35.790
those between the top 1% and the top 10% and
meanwhile the minimum wage hasn't even kept

00:04:35.790 --> 00:04:37.310
up with inflation.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.470
Okay.

00:04:38.470 --> 00:04:45.080
Understand the sick hypocrisy and crony bottom
feeding pond scum nonsense of this.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:49.550
They say emergency, we've got to index capital
gains to inflation.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:53.610
Meanwhile, the minimum wage hasn't kept up
with inflation.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:05:00.130
The bottom half of America hasn't seen in
real terms, wage increase in decades.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.310
What is it 30 or 40 years?

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:07.760
That's not an emergency, but indexing capital
gains to inflation is such a problem, such

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:13.780
an emergency that immediately we need to go
outside of the normal legislative process

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:16.139
and get an executive order in place.

00:05:16.139 --> 00:05:18.090
These people are immoral.

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:19.090
That's it.

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:23.070
I mean, Ted Cruz has to be voted out, but
Ted Cruz is just a symptom of the disease.

00:05:23.070 --> 00:06:49.460
It's way bigger than Ted Cruz.

